          "text": "{\"relation\":\"REFINED\",\"consensus_summary\":\"Swine symbolize uncleanness or impurity and, by extension, profane, sinful, apostate, or spiritually unreceptive people.\",\"book_summary\":\"Swine signify hypocritical covenant claimants: people or a religious kingdom possessing an outward covenant sign but lacking inward spiritual reality, especially those identified as the “synagogue of Satan.”\",\"consensus_core_identification\":\"The unclean or spiritually profane.\",\"book_core_identification\":\"Outwardly covenantal but inwardly unclean religious pretenders.\",\"core_relation\":\"BOOK_NARROWS\",\"extension_relation\":\"BOOK_SUBSET\",\"boundary_disagreement\":\"The consensus applies swine broadly to impurity, profane persons, apostates, pagans, sensuality, and related forms of degradation. The book restricts the controlling identification to persons or corporate religious bodies that claim covenant status outwardly while lacking its inward reality. Thus ordinary sinners, pagans, or impure persons are not necessarily swine under the book’s defining condition.\",\"material_contradiction\":\"There is no direct contradiction at the core: the book retains uncleanness and profanation but specifies a narrower kind of uncleanness—religious hypocrisy and false covenant identity. Its identification of the gathered referent with the “synagogue of Satan” goes beyond, rather than replaces, the consensus category.\",\"rationale\":\"The book’s interpretation is recognizable within consensus alternatives such as hypocrisy, superficial morality, heresy, apostasy, and those who trample sacred things. It nevertheless makes the divided hoof without cud-chewing into a precise outward-versus-inward covenant schema and applies it corporately to false claimants to Jewish identity. That materially narrows the broad consensus extension while preserving its central category of spiritual uncleanness.\",\"citation_support\":\"PARTIAL\",\"strongest_objection\":\"Leviticus 11:7 explicitly establishes the pig’s uncleanness, and Matthew 7:6 and 2 Peter 2:22 support trampling holiness and returning to filth. However, none of the printed texts explicitly identifies swine with outward covenant signs, false Jews, or the “synagogue of Satan.” Matthew 23, Romans 2, and Revelation 2–3 establish outward/inward hypocrisy and false covenant claims independently, so their fusion with swine remains an inferred typological synthesis.\",\"confidence\":\"high\"}"
        }
      ],
